From 0c86480bf18039342b2dd468764206968a9cda9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] tests: kernel: mutex: match thread entries to
 k_thread_entry_t

The complex priority inversion test declares its participant threads as
void f(struct k_sem *, struct k_sem *) and casts them to
k_thread_entry_t, which the kernel calls with three void * arguments.
Calling a function through an incompatible function type is undefined
behaviour, and it traps on targets that check indirect calls.

Take the three void * arguments and convert the two semaphores inside,
and drop the cast that hid the mismatch.

Assisted-by: Claude:MODEL-VERSION
